    "body": "#### vim-patch:b6e2830: runtime(netrw): E118 when netrw#Obtain() rejects a hostname\n\nProblem:  netrw#Obtain() passes the hostname to netrw#msg#Notify() as a\n          third argument, so instead of \"Rejecting invalid hostname\"\n          the user gets E118: Too many arguments for function.\nSolution: Format the message with printf() first, as the other\n          \"Rejecting invalid hostname\" messages in netrw already do.\n\nrelated: vim/vim#21534\n\nhttps://github.com/vim/vim/commit/b6e28306e30eccb25f0dbc772f6fe0a891ac1466\n\nCo-authored-by: Yoko Davis <56965728+revesis@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n\n#### vim-patch:9810654: runtime(netrw): \"O\" in a local listing does not copy the file\n\nProblem:  Pressing \"O\" in a local listing reports \"cannot determine\n          method\" instead of copying the file to the current directory\n          as documented in |netrw-O|.\nSolution: Use the islocal argument of netrw#Obtain() instead of\n          b:netrw_islocal, and copy the files from b:netrw_curdir.\n\nb:netrw_islocal is only set when a file is marked while other files are\nalready marked, so without marks netrw#Obtain() took the remote branch.\nThe names in the listing are relative to b:netrw_curdir, which is not\nvim's current directory when netrw obtains a file, so the local copy\ncommand could not find them.\n\nrelated: vim/vim#21534\n\nhttps://github.com/vim/vim/commit/98106548d042dde9344ec10fd24203d4a2199522\n\nCo-authored-by: Yoko Davis <56965728+revesis@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n\n#### vim-patch:7a5211d: runtime(netrw): \"O\" in a local listing fails on MS-Windows\n\nProblem:  On MS-Windows, \"O\" in a local listing does not copy the file,\n          Test_netrw_obtain_local() fails with E484.  \"cmd /c copy\" does\n          not handle the composed source and target paths.\nSolution: Use filecopy() for each file, as s:NetrwMarkFileCopy() does.\n\ncloses: vim/vim#21534\n\nhttps://github.com/vim/vim/commit/7a5211d6b17ae669946e84cba6b25f72da7d7b5a\n\nCo-authored-by: Yoko Davis <56965728+revesis@users.noreply.github.com>",
